title: Part of a Faction Threatens to Leave
subtitle: A faction's dissent has reached 60 over a concrete demand.
new-page: true
tags: pl_event
face-image: img/polish/polish_event_faction_split.jpg
view-if: {! return !!Q.S && !!Q.polish_party_rules && PolishParty.factionSplitDue(Q) !}
on-arrival: {!
// Event party.faction_split, E3 (technical reference 10.2, 17.15; card catalogue 9.10; Z — 0.38): one
// definition for every faction, one instance per faction case. Two choices, a mandatory answer of 0 T. The
// demand takes back the recorded cause with the largest share of the dissent (decision 3A of stage 5).
PolishParty.factionSplitView(Q);
!}

= Part of [+ pl_e3_faction +] threatens to leave

The dissent of [+ pl_e3_faction +] is [+ pl_e3_dissent +]. Its leaders demand that PPS [+ pl_e3_demand +]. If PPS keeps its line: [+ pl_e3_preview +]

- @accept
- @refuse

@accept
title: Accept the demand and keep unity
subtitle: PPS makes the change at once, without cost; the faction's dissent −5. Partners react to the changed policy itself.
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.factionSplitAccept(Q);
!}
go-to: result

@refuse
title: Keep the line of PPS and accept the split
subtitle: 40% of the faction's base leaves with its voters and MPs; the rest of the faction's dissent −20.
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.factionSplitRefuse(Q);
!}
go-to: result

@result
new-page: true

= The faction's answer

[+ pl_party_result +]

- @root: Continue.
